+// Dark pop contact assist. A recording of dark pop attempts showed the game decides between "pop" and
+// "bail" at the tick where it raises the landing request in the skater's request block (context+0x13c8,
+// bits 0xe000000): if the landing-contact flag (context+0x13cc, bit 0x400) is already set it bails, if it is
+// not it pops. Letting go of the D-pad early lets the contact flag settle first. While enabled, and the
+// D-pad Right was pressed within the last 1.2 s, the contact flag is cleared on the tick the landing stage
+// (request bit 0x4000000) shows, so the pop request is judged first. Publish from the client tick.
+void contact_assist_update(bool enabled, bool dpad_down) noexcept;
+std::uint64_t contact_assist_count() noexcept; // contact flags cleared since the process started
 // Stopping flight must not discard the independent manual preference.
 void clear_no_bail_flight() noexcept;
